---
code: K0038
title: Function Name Not Kebab-Case
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, naming-convention, kebab-case, function]
description: "Function name must be formatted in kebab-case"
---

Function names in Kura must use `kebab-case` (lowercase letters, digits, and single `-` separators, such as `render-header` or `compute-offset`). Uppercase characters (`camelCase` or `PascalCase`) and `snake_case` underscores are rejected.

## Example

This error occurs when a function is declared with uppercase letters or underscores:

```kura
fn renderHeader() => #text("Welcome")

fn compute_offset(x: Int): Int => x + 4
```

## Solution

Rename the function using lowercase `kebab-case`:

```kura
fn render-header() => #text("Welcome")

fn compute-offset(x: Int): Int => x + 4
```
